  "$comment": [
    "The CLOSED set of product-owned managed-capability CONTRACT CATALOGUES this repository may publish.",
    "A contract catalogue is a stateless-protocol-adapter by governed extraction shape, but earns this stricter release profile only when its installed wheel exports one ProductManifestSnapshot plus exact owned CapabilityContractSnapshot and CapabilitySchemaDocument bytes, or an exact CapabilityCompositionSnapshot with separately named, exact dependency documents.",
    "It owns no provider I/O, connector entry point, secret, persistence, retry engine or deployment decision. The contract package describes product semantics; an independently released connector implements them.",
    "Only the complete owner catalogues admitted by ADR-0034 and their exact-pinned composition catalogues belong here. Every absent owner catalogue remains publication-locked."
